2. Citation

When you publicly report research that used this software, cite the software and credit Jimi Goldstein and any other authors identified for the release. This applies to papers, preprints, theses, public reports and presentations. Use the citation supplied with the release, for example in CITATION.cff, and identify the version or commit you used. If the release supplies no citation, give the software title, Jimi Goldstein and any other credited authors, the version or commit, and the repository URL or DOI.

3. Sharing research copies

You may share the original or modified software with others for noncommercial research. Include this licence and the existing copyright and attribution notices with each copy. Identify any changes you made and provide your modifications to recipients under these same terms.

